ildren":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Outlook it expresses"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"direction-neutral, expecting little movement"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Opens with"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"a credit"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Best case"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"Total premium received, anywhere between the two strikes"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Worst case"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"Unlimited on the upside, very large on the downside"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Breakeven"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"Upper strike plus total premium, and lower strike minus total premium"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Exposures"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"delta neutral · gamma negative · theta positive · vega negative"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-card border px-[18px] py-4 transition-colors duration-panel ease-standard bg-card border-border shadow-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-3 flex items-center gap-2","children":["$undefined",["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-base font-semibold leading-tight","children":["Lesson",false]}],false]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted [&_h1]:mb-2 [&_h1]:text-base [&_h1]:font-bold [&_h1]:text-text [&_h2]:mb-1.5 [&_h2]:mt-5 [&_h2]:text-[13px] [&_h2]:font-bold [&_h2]:text-text [&_h3]:mb-1 [&_h3]:mt-4 [&_h3]:text-[12px] [&_h3]:font-semibold [&_h3]:text-text [&_p]:mb-2.5 [&_strong]:font-semibold [&_strong]:text-text [&_ul]:mb-2.5 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-5 [&_ol]:mb-2.5 [&_ol]:list-decimal [&_ol]:pl-5 [&_li]:mb-1 [&_code]:rounded [&_code]:bg-bg [&_code]:px-1 [&_code]:py-0.5 [&_code]:font-mono [&_code]:text-[11px] [&_code]:text-text [&_table]:mb-3 [&_table]:w-full [&_table]:text-left [&_table]:text-[11.5px] [&_th]:border-b [&_th]:border-border [&_th]:pb-1 [&_th]:pr-3 [&_th]:font-semibold [&_th]:text-text [&_td]:border-b [&_td]:border-border [&_td]:py-1 [&_td]:pr-3 [&_td]:align-top [&_a]:text-teal hover:[&_a]:underline [&_blockquote]:border-l-2 [&_blockquote]:border-border2 [&_blockquote]:pl-3 [&_blockquote]:italic","children":[["$","h1","h1-0",{"children":"Short Strangle"}],"\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":"A short out-of-the-money call and a short out-of-the-money put, same expiry. The\r\nmost widely used undefined-risk premium-selling structure in the Indian retail\r\nmarket."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-0",{"children":"The structure"}],"\n",["$","p","p-1",{"children":"Two short legs, both out of the money. Premium from both is credited. Margin is\r\nblocked on both legs, though exchanges grant some offset for the opposing\r\ndirectional exposure."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-1",{"children":"What it is exposed to"}],"\n",["$","p","p-2",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Theta"}]," positive across a wide price range — the structural attraction. Unlike\r\na short straddle, which realises maximum profit at exactly one price, a short\r\nstrangle realises maximum profit anywhere between its strikes. That wide\r\nprofit plateau is what makes it feel safer than it is."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-3",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Gamma"}]," negative, low while the underlying sits mid-range, rising sharply as\r\nprice approaches either strike. The risk is not uniform across the position's\r\nlife: it is negligible for most of the holding period and then concentrated."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-4",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Vega"}]," negative. A volatility expansion damages both legs at once."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-2",{"children":"Why the wide plateau is misleading"}],"\n",["$","p","p-5",{"children":"The payoff diagram's flat top spans a wide range, which reads as a large margin\r\nof safety. What the diagram does not show is that the position's risk is not\r\ndistributed across that range — it is entirely in the tails, and the tails are\r\nwhere the position has no defined loss."}],"\n",["$","p","p-6",{"children":"A short strangle's profit is capped and known. Its loss is neither. The wide\r\nplateau increases the probability of the capped outcome without changing the\r\nmagnitude of the uncapped one."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-3",{"children":"Indian market specifics"}],"\n",["$","p","p-7",{"children":"Every structural rule that applies to the short straddle applies here."}],"\n",["$","p","p-8",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Expiry-day extreme loss margin"}]," of 2% on short options, since November 2024."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-9",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Calendar-spread margin benefit withdrawn on expiry day"}],", February 2025 — a\r\nstrangle margin-offset by longer-dated positions loses that offset on expiry\r\nday."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-10",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Intraday position-limit monitoring"}]," at multiple snapshots since April 2025."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-11",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Contract-value floor."}]," SEBI's November 2024 increase of minimum index\r\ncontract value to ₹15–20 lakh means a single strangle's notional exposure is\r\nsubstantial. The margin blocked is a fraction of that notional; the loss in a\r\ntail move is not."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-12",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Gap risk"}]," is the dominant hazard. Both legs are exposed overnight. An\r\nopening gap beyond a strike converts a comfortable position into a large loss\r\nwith no intervening opportunity to act."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-13",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Skew."}]," The put leg collects more premium than the equidistant call leg.\r\nSelecting strikes by equal premium rather than equal distance places the put\r\nstrike further from spot than the call — a materially different risk\r\ndistribution from the symmetric version, and generally the more considered\r\nconstruction."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-14",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Physical settlement"}]," on stock strangles: whichever leg finishes in the money\r\ncreates a full-contract-value obligation on E+2."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-4",{"children":"The defined-risk equivalent"}],"\n",["$","p","p-15",{"children":["An iron condor is a short strangle with further-out wings bought on both sides.\r\nIt collects less premium, caps the loss at the wing width, and reduces margin\r\nsubstantially. The comparison between the two is the central capital-allocation\r\nquestion in premium selling, and is set out in\r\n",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"strategies/volatility/iron-condor.md"}],"."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-5",{"children":"How it typically fails"}],"\n",["$","p","p-16",{"children":"Long sequences of full-premium expiries, size scaled to that experience, and a\r\nsingle gap or volatility expansion that removes more than the sequence\r\ncontributed. The structure's reliability is real; it is the loss distribution\r\nthat is misread, not the win rate."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-6",{"children":"Related"}],"\n",["$","ul","ul-0",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"strategies/volatility/iron-condor.md"}]," — the defined-risk version"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"strategies/volatility/short-straddle.md"}]," — narrower, more theta, more gamma"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"risk/position-sizing.md"}]," — sizing against notional rather than margin"]}],"\n"]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[10px] leading-relaxed text-faint","children":["Educational material describing how a structure behaves. Not a recommendation, not a signal, and not personalised advice. Source: ",["$","code",null,{"className":"font-mono","children":"docs/learning/strategies/volatility/short-strangle.md"}]]}]]}],null],null],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children","strategy","children","$4","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children","strategy","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[[null,["$","$L6",null,{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":[["$","title",null,{"chil